/*  FUNCTION NAME:      FINDFIRST
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Returns the first non-sentinel answer from applying a predicate to each case. Predicate signature: LAMBDA(case, i) returning the answer, or the sentinel for no match.*/
/*  RETURNS:            value: the first non-sentinel answer from the predicate (or if_not_found)
    PARAMETERS:
        cases           (Required) Array of case tokens. Vertical or horizontal — flattened with TOCOL.
        predicate       (Required) LAMBDA(case, i) returning the answer, or no_match for a miss. i is 1-based.
        if_not_found    (Optional) Value to return when every case missed. Defaults to no_match.
        no_match        (Optional) Sentinel value the predicate returns for no-match. Defaults to "". Override when "" is a valid answer.
    EXAMPLE:            =FINDFIRST({"a";"b";"c"}, LAMBDA(cur, i, IF(cur="b", "found-" & i, ""))) -> "found-2"
    NOTE:               Predicate must take exactly two args — LAMBDA(case, i) — even if i is unused. A one-arg predicate silently returns no matches because every call errors and is caught as a miss. To diagnose, MAP the predicate over the cases yourself and look for #VALUE! in every row.
    NOTE:               Excel REDUCE has no real short-circuit, so all predicates are evaluated regardless. The sentinel is compared with `<>` so it must be a comparable value (text, number, boolean) — not NA() or another error. Errors thrown inside the predicate are caught and treated as a miss.
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-05-02  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Make sentinel customisable (no_match) + add if_not_found return; accept horizontal or vertical cases
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Swap arg order: if_not_found before no_match (more commonly customised)
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Treat predicate errors as a miss instead of poisoning the whole result
                        2026-05-03  Claude      Add DEBUGGING help line calling out the 2-arg predicate gotcha
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
FINDFIRST = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [cases],
    [predicate],
    [if_not_found],
    [no_match],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        sentinel, IF(ISOMITTED(no_match), "", no_match),
        notFound, IF(ISOMITTED(if_not_found), sentinel, if_not_found),
        flat, TOCOL(cases),
        n, ROWS(flat),
        answers, MAP(flat, SEQUENCE(n), LAMBDA(cur, i, IFERROR(predicate(cur, i), sentinel))),
        matches, IFERROR(FILTER(answers, answers <> sentinel, sentinel), sentinel),
        first, INDEX(matches, 1),
        result, IF(@first = sentinel, notFound, first),
        result
)
);
